<title>UK: GOLF-WORLD RANKINGS.</title>
<headline>GOLF-WORLD RANKINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealander Frank Nobilo's</p>
<p>successful defence of his Sarazen World Open title in Georgia on</p>
<p>Sunday boosted him four places to 29th spot in the world</p>
<p>rankings issued on Monday.</p>
<p>Tournament runner-up Scott Hoch moved up two positions to</p>
<p>18th place while in the top five, Briton Nick Faldo overhauled</p>
<p>Fred Couples in fourth place.</p>
<p>Top 20:</p>
<p> 1. Greg Norman (Australia)		     10.38 points average</p>
<p> 2. Tom Lehman (U.S.)				9.46</p>
<p> 3. Ernie Els (South Africa)		     8.77</p>
<p> 4. Nick Faldo (England)			   8.66</p>
<p> 5. Fred Couples (U.S.)			    8.58</p>
<p> 6. Colin Montgomerie (Scotland)		 8.33</p>
<p> 7. Masashi Ozaki (Japan)			  8.18</p>
<p> 8. Phil Mickelson (U.S.)			  7.74</p>
<p> 9. Corey Pavin (U.S.)			     7.46</p>
<p> 10. Davis Love III (U.S.)			 7.29</p>
<p> 11. Mark O'Meara (U.S.)			   7.10</p>
<p> 12. Nick Price (Zimbabwe)			 6.56</p>
<p> 13. Steve Stricker (U.S.)			 6.11</p>
<p> 14. Steve Elkington (Australia)		 5.83</p>
<p> 15. Bernhard Langer (Germany)		   5.70</p>
<p> 16. Scott Hoch (U.S.)			     5.60</p>
